<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Monastic Community of Mount Athos</h1><p class="st-meta">963 CE – present (approx.) · capital Karyes</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Self-governing Orthodox monastic republic on the Athos peninsula in northern Greece, continuously inhabited by monks for over a thousand years.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hermits lived on the mountainous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Athos</a> peninsula from at least the 9th century. In 963 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athanasios-the-athonite">Athanasios the Athonite</a>, with the backing of his friend the general and future emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-phokas">Nikephoros Phokas</a>, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lavra">Great Lavra</a>, the first large monastery. The first charter, the Tragos, issued under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-tzimiskes">John Tzimiskes</a> around 972, organised the community under a Protos at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karyes">Karyes</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Twenty ruling monasteries, Greek, Serbian (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hilandar">Hilandar</a>), Russian (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-panteleimon-monastery">Saint Panteleimon</a>), Bulgarian (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zograf-monastery">Zograf</a>) and others, own the land and send representatives to the Holy Community at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karyes">Karyes</a>. Women have been excluded since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Life follows the Byzantine liturgical calendar and day, and the monasteries hold great libraries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> and icons.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-athos">Athos</a> kept its autonomy under Byzantine, Serbian and Ottoman rulers. Greek forces took it in 1912, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-lausanne">Treaty of Lausanne</a> and the Greek constitution of 1927 confirmed its self-government under Greek <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>, with a civil governor. It is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/monastic-community-of-mount-athos.jpg" alt="Monastic Community of Mount Athos" width="320" height="212"><figcaption>Image: Stavros Stavrakis · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%CE%99%CE%B5%CF%81%CE%AC_%CE%A0%CE%B1%CF%84%CF%81%CE%B9%CE%B1%CF%81%CF%87%CE%B9%CE%BA%CE%AE_%CE%BA%CE%B1%CE%B9_%CE%A3%CF%84%CE%B1%CF%85%CF%81%CE%BF%CF%80%CE%B7%CE%B3%CE%B9%CE%B1%CE%BA%CE%AE_%CE%9C%CE%BF%CE%BD%CE%AE_%CE%93%CF%81%CE%B7%CE%B3%CE%BF%CF%81%CE%AF%CE%BF%CF%85_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>963 CE – present (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Karyes</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Athanasios the Athonite</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Mount Athos, Agion Oros, Holy Mountain</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1494&amp;focus=monastic-community-of-mount-athos" aria-label="Monastic Community of Mount Athos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5276 738 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Monastic Community of Mount Athos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5596 994L5709 970M5596 994L5521 939M5596 994L5709 970M5596 994L5591 1068M5596 994L5591 1068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5709 970h0M5521 939h0M5709 970h0M5591 1068h0M5591 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5596 994h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5596 994h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Karyes. <a href="/atlas?year=1494&amp;focus=monastic